  "finding": "The separate Nereus native IPv6 preload, presently mapped by SmartSDR, deadlocks a nested close() from a signal handler when interrupted while its outer close() holds the state mutex.",
  "scope": "Deterministic fixture reproduces this behavior in the exact installed ARM64 shared library, in a separate capability-free UID78666/GID20/NNP1 process at nice19. No firmware signal handler or original reboot failure was reproduced.",
  "test_design": {
    "trigger": "A second test-only preload raises SIGUSR1 at the underlying-close boundary, after the IPv6 wrapper has taken its mutex. The handler closes a different /dev/null descriptor. Neither descriptor is a socket or firmware resource.",
    "control": "Test hook without the IPv6 library; same handler returns.",
    "timeout": "In-process one-second SIGALRM exits124 using _exit; parent has a separate three-second timeout. Observed result124 includes handler_entered and deadline, not a parent timeout.",
    "privilege_admission": "Fixture itself verifies UID/eUID78666, GID/eGID20, all five capability sets zero and NoNewPrivs1 before arming the trigger.",
